From 94569c3a3f8934306c23b2e3bed16a9e2ae3cc45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Jose M. Caballero Guerrero"
 <80172778+Caballero-git@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:23:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 29/30] media: i2c: add GalaxyCore GC02M2 sensor driver

Driver for the GalaxyCore GC02M2, the 2 MP front camera of the Teclast
P25T: 1600x1200 raw Bayer, 1 MIPI CSI-2 lane at 672 Mbps (link frequency
336 MHz), 24 MHz MCLK, I2C address 0x10, chip ID 0x02f0.

Register table, gain table and power-on order come from Rockchip's BSP
driver gc02m2.c (2020, V0.0X01.0X02). Written for mainline: CCI register
access (8-bit registers, page select 0xfe), subdev state and streams,
runtime PM with autosuspend, MCLK, three supplies and optional reset and
powerdown GPIOs from the device tree. 16-bit values are written as two
8-bit registers, as the BSP driver does.

Modes: 1600x1200 and a centred 1296x972 crop (same size as the rear
camera's binned mode), both at the BSP frame timing (HTS 2192, VTS
1268). Controls: exposure, analogue gain (total gain in 1/64, analogue
step + digital pre-gain as in the BSP), vblank, hblank, pixel rate, link
frequency, horizontal/vertical flip (page 0 register 0x17; not while
streaming), orientation/rotation from the DT.

The Bayer order is RGGB with any flip: the sensor moves its readout by a
row/column when flipping, so the green pixels stay on the anti-diagonal
of each 2x2 cell (checked with all four flip combinations).

P25T tests: p25t-sway tests/ 07-10 (by hand, before the driver), 11-21.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
